 <h1>Exercise Name: Pec Deck Fly / Machine Chest Fly</h1>
  <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>
This 3D anatomical animation demonstrates the Pec Deck Fly (Machine Chest Fly) with a focus on optimal seat setup and arm alignment. The video uses glowing anatomical highlights on the chest (Pectoralis Major) to show how adjusting seat height so that your arms press forward directly inline with mid-chest level creates maximal engagement across the main pectoral fibers.

 Exercise Name: Pec Deck Fly / Machine Chest Fly<br>
 Target Muscles: Mid-to-Overall Chest (Pectoralis Major)<br>
 Secondary Muscles: Anterior Deltoids (front shoulders), Serratus Anterior<br>
</div></div>
<pre>

<h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1>

 <u><b><h4>Seat Height Setup</h4></b></u>: Adjust the seat height so the handles align directly with mid-chest level (shown with the green alignment arrow in the video). Your upper arms should stay horizontal and perpendicular to your torso.
 <u><b><h4>Grip & Position</h4></b></u>: Sit with your back flat against the backrest and plant your feet firmly on the floor. Hold the handles with a neutral grip while keeping a soft, constant bend in your elbows.
 <u><b><h4>Fly Phase (Concentric)</h4></b></u>: Exhale as you bring the handles together in a controlled arc in front of your chest until they meet in the center. Focus on squeezing your pecs together.
 <u><b><h4>Return Phase (Eccentric)</h4></b></u>: Inhale as you slowly control the weight back outward, opening your chest until you feel a complete stretch across your pecs before starting the next rep.



<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Direct Pec Isolation:</b> Isolates the chest muscles completely without tricep involvement, making it an excellent finisher or hypertrophy exercise.
 <b>◉Constant Mechanical Tension:</b> Ensures smooth, continuous resistance through the full range of motion, including the fully squeezed peak position.
 <b>◉Shoulder Safety & Guidance:</b> Fixed machine path provides high stability, making it safer for the shoulders than heavy free-weight dumbbell flyes.


<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep your chest proud and shoulders pressed back against the pad to prevent your front shoulders from overriding the chest work.
